   "summary": "The concluding pages argue that the Nippon Bank should manage currency, resources, storehouses, and emergency taxation, while state-recognized syndicates direct enterprises and reward productive efficiency. The author proposes a promoted labor force organized as an “industrial army corps” and loans to help tenant farmers buy land. A strengthened National Service Association, built on community and town assemblies, would coordinate distribution, local welfare, and public morale.",
